# Other Aerospace Engineering Projects

This section contains two multidisciplinary MSc projects at **Politecnico di Milano**, covering high-speed aerodynamics, CFD and launch-system design.

## SR-71 Inlet CFD Study

A five-member team investigated the mixed-compression inlet across multiple supersonic Mach regimes using **SU2**, including inviscid and RANS modelling, mesh-convergence studies and validation against reference data.

My contribution formed part of the numerical-analysis and technical-reporting workflow, with emphasis on understanding shock structure, pressure recovery and the limits of the modelling approach.

## JEENO — Air-Launched Orbital System

JEENO was a nine-member preliminary design study of a reusable air-launched two-stage orbital vehicle.

My primary responsibility was the **aerodynamic subsystem**. I worked on aerodynamic modelling, lift and drag estimation, centre-of-pressure and stability analysis, fin sizing, high-Mach modelling and validation against independent aerospace tools. The aerodynamic model was integrated with trajectory, structures, propulsion and recovery analyses.
